==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[ab init]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|ab||from}} + {{m|la|initiō}}, ablative singular of {{m|la|initium||beginning}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌæb ɪˈnɪʃ.i.oʊ/|/ˌæb əˈnɪt.i.oʊ/|/ˌɑb əˈnɪt.i.oʊ/|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{head|en|adverb|head=ab initio}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} From the time when a law, legal right or decree, contract, ownership interest, partnership (etc.) comes into force. {{defdate|Early 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref>http://karnatakajudiciary.kar.nic.in/hcklibrary/PDF/Blacks%20Law%206th%20Edition%20-%20SecA.pdf Black's Law Dictionary, 6th Edition (1990) ''Ab initio'': Lat. From the beginning; from the first act; from the inception. An agreement is said to be "void ab initio" if it has at no time had any
legal validity. A party may be said to be a trespasser, an estate said to be good, an agreement or deed said to
be void, or a marriage or act said to be unlawful, ab initio. Contrasted in this sense with ex post facto, or
with postea.</ref><ref>{{R:SOED5|page=4}}</ref><ref>{{w|Black's Law Dictionary}}</ref>
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2007|author=w:Parliament of India|title=w:Prohibition of Child Marriage Act, 2006|chapter=Section 14|url=https://socialwelfare.assam.gov.in/sites/default/files/swf_utility_folder/departments/sw_webcomindia_org_oid_3/menu/document/prohibition_of_child_marriage_act.pdf|page=4|text=Any [[child marriage]] [[solemnise]]d in contravention of an [[injunction]] order issued under section 13, whether [[interim]] or final, shall be void '''''ab initio'''''.}}
# {{lb|en|science}} Calculated from first principles, i.e. from basic laws without any further additional assumptions.
#* '''1983''', Monty Python, ''[[w:Monty Python's The Meaning of Life|The meaning of life]]'', at about 1h 15':
#*: {{...}} this soul does not exist '''''ab initio''''', as orthodox Christianity teaches; it has to be brought into existence by a process of guided self-observation. However, this is rarely achieved, owing to man's unique ability to be distracted from spiritual matters by everyday trivia.
# {{lb|en|of an academic course}} Taken with no prior qualifications.

